Emulate glLineWidth > 1 as screen-space quads on stacks whose
GL_ALIASED_LINE_WIDTH_RANGE is [1, 1] (ANGLE / WebGL).

gl4es_glLineWidth already flushes pending immediate batches via
PUSH_IF_COMPILING and mirrors the value for Get/PushAttrib. It does
not change a pixel on WebGL. This patch expands each segment into a
clip-space quad at draw time and draws it with a temporary identity
MVP (the helper from gl4es-polygon-offset-line.patch), so
gl_Position = MVP * clip becomes a passthrough and depth stays
perspective-correct.

- expand_wide_lines in line.c: 4D near-plane clip (z+w=0), pixel-space
  2D perpendicular, square caps, GL_LINE_LOOP close (which
  gen_stipple_tex_coords skips). Cached object-space line_arrays are
  never written.
- listdraw.c hooks *before* line_arrays_to_vbo (and therefore before
  listActiveVBO). The object-space VBO is not uploaded or bound for
  the wide frame. Stipple generation bumps list->maxtex so the
  expander sees the generated s coordinate.
- drawing.c intercepts GL_LINES / LINE_STRIP / LINE_LOOP so
  client-array draws cannot sneak past (from_polygon_mode = 0).
- Polygon-mode edges with GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_LINE get GLES FILL offset
  on the quads; genuine line primitives force FILL off. The
  prerequisite's projection-row bias is skipped on this path.
- Getter range lives in each glGet* switch (not commonGet): [1, 64]
  when maxlinewidth==1. Granularity 1.0 lives in commonGet.
- Same-width early-out stays after PUSH_IF_COMPILING on both
  glLineWidth and glLineWidthx (16.16 -> float). Compiled
  STAGE_GLCALL glLineWidth already replays before geometry on the
  same node; no linewidth_op.
- wide_ensure allocates newly required attribute buffers even when
  the vertex capacity is already large enough (global scratch is
  shared across draws).
- Degenerate segments use the same half-extent as the ribbon
  (width/2 pixels each side) and emit a real square.

Width 1 stays on the cheap DrawArrays(GL_LINES) path. Fog, lighting,
and clip-plane scenes skip or disable those on the expanded draw
(known deviations). Tessellation overlays that use genuine
GL_LINE_LOOP are not pulled forward -- native _LINE never applied
to them.

Applied last in GL4ES_PATCHES.
